{"key": "KXAMERICAPROFIT|Will America profit in any month of 2025?|If the Monthly Treasury Statement (MTS) reports a surplus for any month in 2025, then the market resolves to Yes. The month surplus can be found in the column labeled \"Current Month Deficit Surplus Amount\" in the the table \"Summary of Receipts, Outlays, and Surplus or Deficit\u201d in the MTS (see: https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/monthly-treasury-statement/summary-of-receipts-outlays-and-the-deficit-surplus-of-the-u-s-government).", "decision": "YES", "confidence": 0.95, "reasoning": "The Monthly Treasury Statement for September 2025 reports a surplus of $198 billion. The resolution criteria explicitly states: \"If the Monthly Treasury Statement (MTS) reports a surplus for any month in 2025, then the market resolves to Yes.\" Since the MTS reports a surplus for September 2025, the condition is met and the market should resolve YES. While some of this surplus included one-time items (student loan reforms and timing shifts), the resolution criteria does not exclude such items - it simply requires that the MTS report a surplus, which it does.", "sources": ["https://www.crfb.org/press-releases/treasury-confirms-1-8-trillion-deficit-fy-2025", "https://seekingalpha.com/news/4504964-u-s-budget-balance-flips-to-198b-surplus-in-september", "https://www.fiscal.treasury.gov/files/reports-statements/mts/mts0925.pdf"], "queries": ["Monthly Treasury Statement 2025 surplus deficit any month", "US Treasury monthly surplus 2025 fiscal data", "\"September 2025\" Treasury surplus $198 billion"], "links": ["https://www.crfb.org/press-releases/treasury-confirms-18-trillion-deficit-fy-2025", "https://www.fiscal.treasury.gov/files/reports-statements/mts/mts0625.pdf", "https://fiscal.treasury.gov/files/reports-statements/mts/mts0825.pdf", "https://fiscal.treasury.gov/files/reports-statements/mts/mts0725.pdf", "https://www.fiscal.treasury.gov/files/reports-statements/mts/mts0125.pdf", "https://fiscal.treasury.gov